      "answer": "[REDACTED] is a typed work-unit queue on an append-only JSONL ledger. Three dispatcher adapters (local, worktree, cloud) compare-and-append a CLAIM record whose named fields are claim_id, fencing_token, lease_until_ns and dedupe_key; fcntl.LOCK_EX serializes the append so two dispatchers racing the same unit produce exactly one WON. Delivery is at-least-once plus idempotent units: exactly-once is not claimed, because a crash after a side effect and before COMPLETE still re-dispatches. A unit is idempotent iff two executions with the same idempotence_key yield the same CRLF-normalized artifact sha256; the architecture-dossier emit shape on this tree is NON-IDEMPOTENT (wall-clock ended_at) and MUST be skipped after SUCCEEDED rather than re-run. ONE completion reducer is TST-0003.evaluate \u2014 imported, not copied. Dynamic fan-out width comes from agentspec.resolve_dynamic_fanout on a schema-validated producer receipt. Barriers are per-unit timeouts (IsolatedPipelineRunner), not join-all. The FIRST construct that is not expressible is dispatcher-local SUCCESS from process exit code 0.",
